The attached image (Fig. 5) illustrates how Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A's flow cytometry plots show the detection and phenotyping of OVA-positive cells, including various DC subpopulations, in lymph nodes one and two days post-injection. Panel B quantifies that Nano-11 significantly increases the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in OVA-containing cells compared to soluble OVA or OVA+AH, indicating enhanced antigen delivery per cell. Panel C demonstrates that Nano-11 also increases the percentage of migratory DCs (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, suggesting specific targeting to these immunopotentiating cells.